<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al Maktoum</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Maktoum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Al Maktoum are the ruling family of Dubai, descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maktoum-bin-butti">Maktoum bin Butti</a>, who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-bu-falasah">Al Bu Falasah</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dubai-creek">Dubai Creek</a> in 1833. Under rulers such as Rashid bin Saeed and his sons they turned Dubai from a pearling and trading town into a global commercial hub. The ruler of Dubai traditionally serves as vice-president and prime minister of the United Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirates</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-maktoum.jpg" alt="Al Maktoum" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Dubai · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_Arms_of_Dubai_(2024).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
